# Project Styling & Layout Guidelines
- The overall theme is very light with an almost white background.
- Maintain the existing light aesthetic; do not apply terminal-style themes to components.
- The only dark-themed exception is the Hall of Fame page, which uses an almost black background.

# Shared UI & Component Rules
- When creating new pages or views, always preserve and wrap them in the existing layout structure to retain the top navbar and live ticker.
- Do not add icons next to descriptions in dropdown navigation layouts.
- In dropdown menus and navigation bars, ensure the "Account" option is placed at the top of the profile dropdown list.
- Never shrink or modify the size of the navbar profile circle icon.
- Maintain clean blue account-style text-only button designs. Strictly no bracket symbols [] or emojis in buttons or main section headers.

# Data & AI Logic Constraints
- Never suggest dropping essential starting positions or players that would leave a roster vacancy (such as dropping a solo defense).
- Use explicit text explanations for component placements instead of referencing user-provided images.
- Use the text labels "Value/Trend" for player metrics instead of a standard dollar sign ($).

# Strict Schema Utilization Instructions
- Always use these exact active tables and property data types when writing TypeScript functions, UI layout components, or custom Supabase mutations.
- The table `public.user_roles` has been completely dropped from the database schema cache. Never generate code targeting it.
- Admin privilege checks must read `profiles.role` and treat a value that strictly equals `admin` as admin access.

# Database A — Primary User, Profile, & Site Management Tables

